// Permit ApproveSale only when the tool's resolved output reports
// `approved: true`. The new idea: clause bodies can read fields
// from `context.output` the same way they read `context.input`,
// and Bool fields are compared with `== true` / `== false`.
//
// Because `output` is optional on tool actions in the schema, the
// reference is guarded with `context has output` so the validator
// is satisfied when no response is attached to the request.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"ApproveSale",
    resource
)
when {
    if context has output then context.output.approved == true else false
};
